    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d490">

                <pb facs="0794" n="698" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg698"/>

                <head>No. 491.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Mr. Peixotto.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-07-22"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 22,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 34.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 33, of the 24th ultimo,
                    has been received. It is learned with regret that justice has been denied to the
                    Hebrews in Roumania. The Department has complied with your suggestion, that an
                    instruction be addressed to certain ministers of the United States in Europe,
                    directing them to employ moral efforts toward inducing the governments to which
                    they are accredited to forward an adjustment of the question.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
